((date 2026-09-22) (slug top-of-funnel-capacity)
 (hypothesis
  "Top-N capacity at the screener: screening_config.max_buy_candidates 20 -> 40, nothing else changed (size, exposure, slots, grade floor untouched). Motivated by the 26y funnel (#2490: 36 % of monsters die at the top-N cut; ranking has no skill, so the cut at 20 is a lottery) and by the settled REJECTs on every breakout-gate width dial. Pre-registered (#2897, merged before any cell ran): realised AND Calmar better than the null at >= 2 of 3 salts -> ACCEPT(mechanism); if the arm-only cohort is >= 80 % losers at every salt -> REJECT as stale-entry breadth. d0 = the null s0 config with --emit-candidates as a funnel diagnostic + build tripwire.")
 (base_scenario
  "top-of-funnel-2026-09-21: t1-topn-40 = a0-pit-null + ((screening_config ((max_buy_candidates 40)))), paired per salt against the committed a0-pit-null-s{0,1,2}-v11 on _v11pit (9,364 entries, 27-entry yearly top-3000 PIT schedule 1999-2025), sweep-funnel @ad5a9e04e (main after #2882), SNAPSHOT_MAX_MMAP_HANDLES=12000, cells 4h48m / 4h16m / 3h59m. d0 tripwire: trades.csv md5 c1352be681e2eea3bf50d5c58a94f8a7 = committed null s0 (byte-identical metrics). V6 = 0 every cell, validator_diff -check V6 exit 0.")
 (window_id top3000-pit-1999-2025-record-26y-3salt) (baseline_label record-pit-null-v11pit)
 (variants
  (
   ((label topn-40-s0) (config_hash max-buy-candidates-40)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.3618) (mean_calmar 0.1056) (mean_return_pct 237.38) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 44.48)))))
   ((label topn-40-s1) (config_hash max-buy-candidates-40)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.4089) (mean_calmar 0.1235) (mean_return_pct 303.97) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 43.84)))))
   ((label topn-40-s2) (config_hash max-buy-candidates-40)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.4145) (mean_calmar 0.1266) (mean_return_pct 329.51) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 44.68)))))
  ))
 (verdict Accept)
 (notes
  "GRID AMENDMENT 2 (2026-09-24, dev/experiments/top-n-grid-2026-09-22 §Verdict — cell 3 = 26y record window on the yearly top-1000 PIT schedule, null + cap 40 x 3 salts, sweep-grid @ad5a9e04e = cells 1-2 build): null 543.1 / 465.6 / 337.3 % (maxDD 32.15 / 31.36 / 31.29, Calmar 0.226 / 0.216 / 0.183) -> ranges 205.8 pp / 0.87 pt, means 448.7 % / 0.208. Cap 40 231.5 / 225.1 / 404.1 % (36.25 / 33.15 / 39.18, 0.128 / 0.137 / 0.161) -> 179.0 pp / 6.04 pt, means 286.9 % / 0.142. DOMINATED (lower mean realised AND lower mean Calmar) and does not tighten (maxDD range ~7x wider). Grid: cell 1 tightens, cell 2 tightens, cell 3 dominated -> the never-dominated clause fails -> cap 40 NOT PROMOTABLE; default stays 20. Classification REJECT-as-default / keep-as-axis (recorded after the result, not pre-registered); the ACCEPT(mechanism) below is unchanged and max_buy_candidates stays a searchable axis. V6: validator_diff exit 1 on s0 and s1 (null holds the IAC/MTCH 2012-03-15 twin, 4-day +$719 per leg); s2 exit 0. Verdict does not rest on the failing pairs: direct effect ~0.07 pp vs a 161.8 pp mean gap, and the arms first diverge 2000-04-04 at every salt, 12 y before the twin. Cohorts: arm-only +$0.19 M / +$0.85 M / +$2.09 M vs null-only +$1.96 M / +$2.81 M / +$1.63 M - the same monster lottery (BBWI-2020, TSLA-2013, AMAT-2020, ANET-2016). The cell-2 tightening did not survive on this schedule, which is consistent with (not proof of) it resting on ADMA 2023-12-19 (absent from top-1000-2023) - cell 3 drops ~2/3 of the names, so the ADMA question is confounded with breadth. The DOMINATED label rests on the two V6-failing pairs (s2 alone is not dominated); NOT-PROMOTABLE holds without them. WHY (hypothesis): on a top-1000 pool ranks 21-40 come from a thinner tail, the ~5-slot book re-draws onto it -> dispersion tightening is BREADTH-DEPENDENT; stop proposing cap-width points as a default. Side note, not a verdict: the top-1000 null (mean 448.7 %, maxDD 31.3-32.2) sits above the cell-1 top-3000 null on the same window - a lead for a breadth-tier question only. Artifacts: top-n-grid-2026-09-22/results/*-1000-* + chain-C3.log. GRID AMENDMENT (2026-09-23, dev/experiments/top-n-grid-2026-09-22, cell 2 = 2019-2025 sub-window on the same PIT schedule, null + cap {30,40,60} x 3 salts, sweep-grid @ad5a9e04e = cell 1 build, V6 diff exit 0 on all 9 pairs): pre-registered dispersion rule (3-salt realised AND maxDD ranges narrower than the null, promote-eligible at >= 2 of 3 grid cells and never dominated). Null 34.4 / -9.5 / 71.3 % (maxDD 43.4 / 48.3 / 43.8): ranges 80.9 pp / 4.9 pt. Cap 40 50.7 / 88.2 / 52.9 % (43.7 / 47.0 / 44.1): 37.4 pp / 3.3 pt, means 63.9 % and Calmar 0.160 vs 32.1 % and 0.084 -> TIGHTENS, not dominated. Cap 30 20.4 / 130.2 / 69.5 %: 109.7 pp -> does NOT tighten. Cap 60 60.2 / 11.4 / -6.7 % (50.0 / 48.6 / 47.9): 66.9 pp / 2.1 pt but mean 21.6 % / Calmar 0.050 -> tightens AND DOMINATED (band sits above the null). Cap 40 has reached 2 of 3 cells (26y + sub-window); cell 3 (top-1000 schedule) pending; NOT promotable yet, default stays 20. Caveats: ADMA 2023-12-19 (+$327k at each cap-40 salt; +$399k at cap 30 s1, +$303k at cap 60 s0) tops the arm-only cohort at cap 40 on all 3 salts, at cap 30 s1 and cap 60 s0 only; cap 60 s2 arm-only 99 trades -$335k = stale-entry breadth (the dial is bounded above); maxDD tightening at cap 40 is 1.6 pt on a 4.9 pt band. Artifacts: top-n-grid-2026-09-22/results/ (#2925 + the follow-up PR). ACCEPT(mechanism) by the pre-registered rule: 2 of 3 salts clear both metrics (s0 237.4/0.106 vs 457.0/0.165 FAIL; s1 304.0/0.123 vs 188.0/0.077 CLEAR; s2 329.5/0.127 vs 152.0/0.069 CLEAR). NOT PROMOTABLE on this surface: one knob value (40), one window, one breadth tier - experiment-flag-discipline R3 + promotion-confirmation.md require the grid first ({30,40,60} x a disjoint 2019-2025 sub-window x a top-1000 schedule cell; promote only if the dispersion property holds in >= 2 of 3 cells). Default stays 20. LEVEL IS A SALT LOTTERY on both sides: cohort sizes identical at every salt (arm-only 280/280/265, null-only 241/298/261, ~36 % of each book) and the arm-only cohort's sign flips (-$0.87M / +$0.88M / +$0.85M vs null-only +$1.34M / +$0.004M / -$0.51M): s0 the null's draw holds the 2020+2025 monster cohorts, s1 the arm's holds ECHO (+$677k of +$0.88M), s2 the arm's holds six $230k+ winners across five years. Never quote +177pp or -220pp as the mechanism. ROBUST PROPERTY IS DISPERSION (n=3, PLAUSIBLE): arm realised 237-330 % (range 93pp) vs null 152-457 % (305pp); arm maxDD 43.8-44.7 (0.9pt) vs null 40.6-53.0 (12.4pt); means 290 vs 266 % and Calmar 0.119 vs 0.104; medians 304 vs 188 %. Three draws cannot separate 'less path-dependent' from 'the null's s0 is the outlier'. MECHANISM: the leak is SLOT POLICY, not screener capacity - d0 (funnel decomposition, results/d0-funnel-decomposition.md): the cap binds in 99.1 % of 1,335 weeks, cuts >= 20 names in 96.3 %, 33.8 A_plus names/week fall at it (admitted = 94 % A_plus, ranking = score then alphabetical), yet the book fills ~28 entries/yr into ~5 slots (concurrency 4.67-4.85 null vs 5.00-5.03 arm). Joining s0's arm-only entries to the null's own cascade (join.awk): 46 % were names the null ADMITTED the Friday before and never filled, 28 % were the marginal ranks 21-40, 25 % older resting orders. Widening re-draws which resting orders trigger first against the slots + cash floor; the marginal names are slightly worse (score 102-103 vs 106-107; winner rate 6.8/8.6/9.1 % vs 10.8/7.7/6.9 %, no robust sign). So #2490's '36 % of monsters die at top-N' is mostly a slot loss: screened, did not win the slot. FORWARD: next lever = slot-fill ordering when admitted > open slots (score, RS, volume ratio - never alphabetical; book spine item 7 supports RS for selection), pre-registered as a screener-ordering dial; not another cap-width point. RUNTIME: 4h48m/4h16m/3h59m at cap 12,000, peak RSS 6.45-6.47 GB; --emit-candidates doubled d0 (7h25m / 7.60 GB) - keep it off verdict cells. Artifacts: top-of-funnel-2026-09-21/results/t1-topn-40-s{0,1,2}-v11-* (+ per-salt reads), d0-* incl. both equity curves and the s0 join CSV, chain-A.log; README §Log + §Verdict."))
